  "note": [
    {
      "text": "Named test objective #4 from this use case's own documentation: 'The PA number returned in the ClaimResponse must be carried forward into the ServiceRequest (referral) and the 837D claim.' PA number TX-MCD-PA-2026-047291 is carried forward here via supportingInfo, continuing the same chain already present on the referral ServiceRequest (Interaction 2) and originating from the ClaimResponse (Interaction 1)."
    },
    {
      "text": "This bills DentaQuest's dental benefit plan directly — a dental-to-dental payer relationship, not a medical benefit. CDT alone (D7210) is what's required here; no CPT crosswalk reasoning applies, unlike UC01's medical-payer direction. This is the second proof point (after UC01's medical-payer direction) that the ODEDentalClaim profile's shape generalizes across payer types."
    },
    {
      "text": "Deliberately excluded, per this profile's own non-financial design: unitPrice, net, total, adjudication. Also deliberately excluded, per this specific interaction's stated scope: Dr. Parker's own separate claim for the original evaluation and radiograph (D0140, D0220) — a parallel billing event not modeled here, since it doesn't involve the referral relationship or this claims-sharing profile."
    }
  ]
